  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "For some reason, the shader fallback system seems to never fallback to a toon shader properly. It always falls back to Standard with 0 smoothness instead.\n\nThe shader is called \"NoeNoe Toon Cutout\". It has a \"_Ramp\" property that I set to a sharp toon ramp, as opposed to a soft one. This ramp should make it immediately obvious that it's falling back to a toon shader, as the lighting will be harsh rather than soft. And yet, the lighting still looks like Standard when shaders are blocked.\n\nHappens in build 751, but has been going on since the shader fallback system was released and out of beta.",
